TTYCHATTER.NCURSES(1)        User Commands        TTYCHATTER.NCURSES(1)

NAME
    ttychatter.ncurses - full-screen terminal chat client for OpenRouter

SYNOPSIS
    ttychatter.ncurses
    ttychatter.ncurses <session_name>
    ttychatter.ncurses --resume <session|session.log|/path/session.log>
    ttychatter.ncurses --list
    ttychatter.ncurses --models [--model-type TYPE]
    ttychatter.ncurses --routers
    ttychatter.ncurses --update-models
    ttychatter.ncurses --test-model <model_id>
    ttychatter.ncurses --doctor
    ttychatter.ncurses --demo
    ttychatter.ncurses --version
    ttychatter.ncurses --loopback-file <path>
    ttychatter.ncurses --help

DESCRIPTION
    ttychatter.ncurses is the primary full-screen terminal interface for the
    ttychatter project. It is designed to make browser interfaces unnecessary
    for text-message-style AI work from a terminal. It talks to OpenRouter by
    default, uses cached model metadata, stores sessions as plain text logs,
    and saves long code blocks as local attachments.

DEMO MODE
    --demo runs ttychatter.ncurses without OpenRouter network calls.

    Demo mode supplies local model metadata and local AI responses. It is
    intended for release-candidate testing, UI testing, model-browser testing,
    attachment extraction testing, session testing, and first-time exploration
    without spending OpenRouter credits or sending fake prompts.

MODEL BROWSER
    The model browser is table-like. It supports typed search, favorites,
    metadata filters, model tests, and sorting. Cached model lists are preferred.
    Updating the model list contacts OpenRouter only after confirmation.

    Keys inside the browser:
        /       Search by typed string.
        b       Toggle favorite/bookmark for the highlighted model.
        o       Cycle model sort method forward.
        O       Cycle model sort method backward.
        f       Open model filter/options screen.
        t       Test highlighted model.
        i       Show model metadata.
        s       Save highlighted model to config.
        Enter   Activate highlighted model for the current run.
        j/k     Move down/up.

ROUTERS AND FIXED MODELS
    OpenRouter exposes both fixed model IDs and router-like entries.  A fixed
    model is a concrete model route.  Entries such as openrouter/auto and
    openrouter/free are provider-defined routing choices.

    In the model menu, choose Router shortcuts to open a dropdown containing:
        openrouter/auto
        openrouter/free
        other cached OpenRouter router entries, when present

    Command-line equivalents:
        ttychatter.ncurses --routers
        ttychatter.ncurses --models --model-type routers
        ttychatter.ncurses --models --model-type fixed
        ttychatter.ncurses --models --model-type free
        ttychatter.ncurses --models --model-type auto

THEMES
    ttychatter.ncurses supports theme/style profiles through the options menu
    and config file:

        THEME=default
        THEME=dim
        THEME=high_contrast
        THEME=mono
        THEME=solarized_dark

    Themes are terminal-attribute profiles. They cannot guarantee exact colors
    on every terminal emulator, but they centralize how user text, AI text,
    placeholders, command bars, headers, and selections are emphasized.

CONTROLS
    F1        Help / command menu.
    F2        Model menu and model browser.
    F3        API key tools.
    F4        Sessions: switch, new chat, rename, delete.
    F5        Options.
    F6        Memory.
    F7        Files / attachments.
    F8        External editor.
    F9        Credits.
    F10       Quit.

    Enter     Sends by default when SEND_INPUT=enter.
    Ctrl+G    Reliable alternate send key.
    Ctrl+T    Quick attach file for the next request.
    j/k       Move in menus, lists, model browser, memory, files, and editor
              screens.

CONFIGURATION
    Config file:
        ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config

    Important keys:
        OPENROUTER_API_KEY
        TTYCHATTER_API_KEY
        API_KEY_GPG_FILE
        CONFIRM_LIVE_SEND=1|0
        MODEL
        DEMO_MODE=1|0
        THEME=default|dim|high_contrast|mono|solarized_dark
        SEND_INPUT=enter|ctrl_g|ctrl_enter
        PROMPT_SESSION_NAME=1|0
        CONTEXT_TURNS
        SESSION_DIR
        ATTACHMENT_DIR
        MODEL_CACHE_FILE
        CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES
        MODEL_FILTER_CHAT_COMPLETIONS
        MODEL_FILTER_REQUIRE_TOKENS
        MODEL_FILTER_HIDE_PREVIEW
        MODEL_TYPE_FILTER=all|routers|fixed|free|auto
        MODEL_MIN_INPUT_TOKENS
        MODEL_MIN_OUTPUT_TOKENS
        MODEL_SORT_ORDER=favorites|type|api|name|display|input-desc|output-desc

DEFAULT DIRECTORIES
    config:      ~/.config/ttychatter/openrouter/config
    sessions:    ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/sessions/
    attachments: ~/.local/share/ttychatter/openrouter/attachments/
    cache:       ~/.cache/ttychatter/openrouter/models.json

ATTACHMENTS
    Short fenced code blocks remain inline. Long fenced code blocks are saved
    into ATTACHMENT_DIR once they meet CODE_ATTACHMENT_MIN_LINES.

LOOPBACK OUTPUT
    ttychatter.ncurses --loopback-file <path>
        Appends each AI response to the named file while the full-screen
        ncurses interface remains active.

VERSION
    ttychatter.ncurses version 0.14.0
